Refused bulk port creation (#172)
================================

Apply this series to the upstream sonic-sairedis gitlink, currently
8b5e2228c7a254bcef706274738d5e215e9fe930. slave.mk applies/pops the series
around package builds; no fork pin or vendor package is changed here.

The guard skips post-create discovery if the SAI created no ports, preserving
per-object failure statuses. The RedisClient guard separately makes an empty
RID-to-VID lookup a no-op instead of issuing an invalid HMGET.

Required companion: kamelnetworks/sonic-swss#9 (orchagent refusal handling and
portsyncd initialization handshake), delivered through shared buildimage#109.
Neither component alone completes buildimage#172. Do not include unsupported
modes in production platform data merely to trigger this path.

Validation:
  git submodule update --init --depth 1 src/sonic-sairedis
  python3 -m unittest discover -s tests -p test_sairedis_patch_series.py -v

The test applies every listed patch to committed source at the gitlink, then
compiles the actual changed method bodies with deterministic dependency fakes.
It covers all-refused/mixed/successful creates, unsupported bulk APIs, non-port
objects, empty input, zero-count Redis lookup and ordinary nonempty lookup.
Removing either guard must reproduce a failure. These checks are lightweight;
they do not replace the full syncd build, sairedis suite or vendor integration.

Before acceptance: CI-built image with both components; on Seastone 2 and
S5232F, verify refused-create runtime and initialization recovery with refused
rows retained, valid sibling ports/PortInitDone/LAGs and services healthy, then
corrected configuration recovery and complete restoration. Root owns those
hardware operations and any restart authorization.

Remove the carried patch after the corresponding upstream fix is in the pin.
